{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And they came upon the city confidently.</b> Rashi explained that they were confident in the strength of the old man, and some say that this 'old man' is Abraham, their ancestor, who prayed on behalf of the sons of Jacob when they would come to Shechem, as Rashi explained in the portion of לֶךְ לְךָ on ״וַיַּעֲבֹר אַבְרָם בָּאָרֶץ עַד מְקוֹם שְׁכֶם״ (Genesis 12:6). And it is possible to explain 'confidently' — they were confident that the Canaanite and the Perizzite would not seek to take vengeance on their account, for they would say: since these entered the religion of the circumcised, they are no longer of us — and they would despair of them."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:31:57.995666011Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}